{title: 569 - Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Pass me [C]not, O [G]gentle [Dm]Savior,
[G]Hear my humble cry;
[G]While [C]on others [G]Thou [Dm]art calling,
[G]Do not pass me by.

Refrain:
[Am/C]Savior, [C]Savior, [G]hear my humble [Dm]cry;
[G]while on [C]others thou art [G]calling,
[Dm]do not [G/D]pass [Dm]me [G]by.

Verse 2:
[G]Let me [C]at thy [G]throne of [Dm]mercy
[G]find a sweet relief,
[G]kneeling [C]there in [G]deep contrition;
[G]help my unbelief.

Verse 3:
[G]Trusting [C]only [G]in thy [Dm]merit,
[G]would I seek thy face;
[G]heal my [C]wounded, [G]broken [Dm]spirit,
[G]save me by thy grace.

Verse 4:
[G]Thou the [C]spring of [G]all my [Dm]comfort,
[G]more than life to me,
[G]whom have [C]I on [G]earth beside thee?
[G]Whom in heaven but thee?
